prop beast creature.health=12
prop beast creature.damage=1.5
prop beast boss.phase=0.5
prop beast boss.summon=4
prop beast boss.summonKind=Creature_Hyena
prop beast boss.speed=1.3
prop beast tint.color=#a0522d
prop beast tint.amount=0.6
prop beast on.defeat=signal||beast\nmessage||The beast falls by the core. Now the beam - the emitter, two mirrors and the reactor panel.

prop mirror1 obj.name=mirror1
prop mirror1 col.mode=box
prop mirror1 on.use=switch|\nmessage||The mirror grinds round a quarter turn.
prop mirror2 obj.name=mirror2
prop mirror2 col.mode=box
prop mirror2 on.use=switch|\nmessage||The mirror grinds round a quarter turn.
prop reactorpanel obj.name=reactorpanel
prop reactorpanel if.laser=!signal|laser
prop reactorpanel on.laser=signal||laser\ngive||story:heartbeam*1\nmessage||The reactor panel drinks the beam. The heart hums awake - and the Seventh lever's light turns green.
prop seventhlever obj.name=seventhlever
prop seventhlever beh.use=Pull the Seventh lever
prop seventhlever if.use=signal|laser\n!signal|stopped
prop seventhlever else.use=message||The Seventh lever is locked. The heart must be woken with light first.
prop seventhlever on.use=signal||stopped\nhide|coreglow\nshow|coldlights\ngive||story:enginestopped*1\ncamera|wellcam|core|6|40\nmessage||The Seventh lever comes down. The core's glow dies, the wheels stop - and all round the ring, the sea runs back out of the well.
prop coreglow obj.name=coreglow
prop coldlights obj.name=coldlights
prop coldlights beh.hidden=1
prop core obj.name=core
prop wellcam obj.name=wellcam
prop emitter obj.name=emitter
note greylast Silas Grey's last log | S. GREY - THE ENGINE, LAST ENTRY\n\nThe beast is dead and the Engine is quiet, and the boss has gone down to the launch without a word to any of us. Twenty years of paying men to follow other people, and he ends with nothing in his hands.\n\nI watched her come up the ramp out of the well with that brass ring. She did not look at me this time.\n\nThe old expedition left a vault in the gauge house off the south-west point. I found its key in the boss's things, years ago, and never told him. Let whoever ends this have it. I am done waiting for other people. The launch leaves at dusk, and I am not on it.
note okalast Nell Okafor's note | N. OKAFOR - THE ENGINE'S EAST SHORE\n\nProfessor, I said I would follow you, and I did. The Albatross's gondola is in this cave; the balloon is in the bay; the engine runs if you swear at it.\n\nIf you are not the professor: she is all right. I saw her come out of the cage on the south rim. I saw the man in the grey coat climb the hill to the north-west and not come down.\n\nWhen it is over, the gondola flies. There is room for three, if one of them is small. Take what you want from the chest. I have made my last spanner for a while. - Nell
note ostrlast Dr. Ostrander's last letter | DR. HAL OSTRANDER - THE GAUGE HOUSE, 1931\n\nWe reached the Engine. Nobody believed we would. The gauge on this wall has drawn the sea for forty days, and every seventh tide the line climbs and does not come down.\n\nWe could not stop it. The lever wants light, and we had only lamps. I have locked our pay and our samples in the vault and given the key to the boy who carries our water, a quiet lad with grey eyes.\n\nTo whoever stopped it: you did what we could not. The sea will go down, a finger's width at a time. Leave the gauge on the wall. Let it draw the line going down.
prop ringtop zone.id=ring_top
prop ringtop zone.radius=4
prop ringtop zone.message=From the ring's top: the well is still, the sea outside calm. The Seventh Tide is over.

quest title=The Seventh Tide
quest intro=The Engine at last. Kett's camp is on the landing in the south. Go ashore.
